Governance maturity assessments help organizations evaluate how effectively governance policies are implemented across Azure environments.

Assessment areas include:

* Identity governance
* Resource organization
* Policy compliance
* Cost governance
* Security implementation
* Documentation
* Automation maturity

For example, organizations with automated policy enforcement generally achieve higher governance maturity than those relying on manual reviews.

A real-life use case is enterprises measuring governance improvements annually to support organizational growth.

Governance assessments identify strengths, weaknesses, and future improvement opportunities.
